the Iranian president's chief of staff  has said Iran and Saudi Arabia should  work together to resolve their problems  tensions have long been high between the  two countries diplomatic relations were  severed after an attack on the Saudi  embassy in Tehran in 2016 dorsa Jabari  has more from Tehran this comes at a  time when Iran finds itself in a  situation where it needs all the friends  it has in this region this is something  the chief of staff alluded to he said  that there is no reason for Iran not to  have good relations with its neighbors  including Saudi Arabia of course Iran  and Saudi have had a very tumultuous  relationship over the past few years and  it began in January of 2016 when a  number of Iranians stormed the Saudi  embassy in Tehran and destroyed what was  inside because they were angry about an  execution of a Shia cleric in Saudi  Arabia since then Saudi officials have  cut diplomatic relations with Tehran and  things have just escalated since then  given the war in Yemen and a number of  other things that have taken place so  there is a sense on the Iranian side  anyways for now that there needs to be a  close look at this relationship and one  of the main sticking points for Iranians  is the war in Yemen they want to see an  end to that as soon as possible and they  say they are ready to go back to  establishing relationship with Saudi  Arabia as soon as that happens and this  statement we heard from rouhani chief of  staff today just highlights how  important Saudi Arabia is for Iran and  of course in the having stability in  this region
 

